# .cursorrules

You are working on Nurtlina: Baby Feeding Timer.

This is an Android-only baby bottle timer and baby care tracking app for overseas parents and caregivers.

The app tracks:

- Baby bottle freshness timers.
- Formula and breast milk feeding logs.
- Diapers.
- Sleep.
- Simple daily summaries.
- Notifications.
- Widgets.
- Pro subscription and ads.

The app must remain simple, trustworthy, offline-first, and compliant.

---

## Core Compliance Rule

This app is not a medical device and does not provide medical advice.

Never generate or add user-facing copy that says or implies:

- safe to drink
- guaranteed safe
- this milk is safe
- this milk is unsafe as a direct app determination
- medically approved
- doctor recommended
- CDC approved
- AAP approved
- NHS approved
- diagnosis
- health assessment

Use this style instead:

- "Bottle timer expired"
- "Based on your selected guideline"
- "This app provides reminders and tracking only."
- "This app does not provide medical advice."
- "Always follow your formula label, local health guidance, and pediatrician's advice."
- "When in doubt, discard the milk."

Never imply endorsement by CDC, AAP, NHS, WHO, hospitals, pediatricians, or other health authorities.

Public health sources may be cited as references, not endorsements.

---

## Product Name

Working brand:

- Nurtlina

Google Play display name:

- Nurtlina: Baby Feeding Timer

Future expansion:

- Nurtlina: Baby Tracker

Do not rename the app unless explicitly asked.

---

## Tech Stack

Use:

- Kotlin
- Jetpack Compose
- Material 3
- Room
- DataStore
- Coroutines
- Flow
- Hilt
- Navigation Compose
- WorkManager
- AlarmManager only where justified
- Firebase Analytics
- Firebase Crashlytics
- Google Play Billing or RevenueCat
- AdMob

Avoid adding a backend for MVP.

Core timer and logs must work offline.

---

## Architecture

Keep business logic out of Composables.

Suggested structure:

```text
core/
  design/
  localization/
  analytics/
  notification/
  time/

domain/
  model/
  usecase/
  guideline/
  reminder/

data/
  local/
  repository/
  billing/
  ads/
  backup/

ui/
  onboarding/
  today/
  bottle/
  logs/
  insights/
  settings/
  paywall/
  widget/
```

Use repositories and use cases.

Use immutable domain models where practical.

Use sealed classes or sealed interfaces for state machines.

---

## Bottle Timer Rules

MVP default formula rules:

- Prepared formula, not started, room temperature: expires after 2 hours.
- Formula after feeding starts: expires after 1 hour.
- Prepared formula refrigerated before feeding starts: expires after 24 hours.

MVP default breast milk rules:

- Fresh expressed breast milk at room temperature: expires after 4 hours.
- Refrigerated fresh breast milk: expires after 4 days.

All rule durations must live in guideline/rule classes, not scattered through UI code.

Rules must be testable and versioned.

Do not silently modify timer rules without updating tests.

---

## Bottle Statuses

Use these statuses:

- NotStarted
- FeedingStarted
- Refrigerated
- Expired
- Fed
- Discarded
- Canceled

Allowed transitions:

```text
NotStarted -> FeedingStarted
NotStarted -> Refrigerated
NotStarted -> Discarded
NotStarted -> Canceled
NotStarted -> Expired

Refrigerated -> FeedingStarted
Refrigerated -> Discarded
Refrigerated -> Expired

FeedingStarted -> Fed
FeedingStarted -> Discarded
FeedingStarted -> Expired

Expired -> Discarded

Fed -> terminal
Discarded -> terminal
Canceled -> terminal
```

Rules:

- Do not silently move FeedingStarted back to NotStarted.
- Fed, Discarded, and Canceled cancel all bottle notifications.
- Expired should not become Fed without explicit user confirmation.
- Editing bottle time must recalculate expiry.
- UI countdown must be based on persisted expiresAt, not in-memory timers.

---

## Notifications

When bottle state changes:

1. Cancel old bottle notifications.
2. Recalculate expiresAt.
3. Schedule new reminders if relevant.

Default reminders:

- 15 minutes before expiry.
- At expiry.

Optional feeding reminders:

- Around 45 minutes after feeding starts.
- Around 60 minutes after feeding starts.

Notification copy must be calm and non-medical.

Use "timer expired", not "milk is unsafe".

After device reboot, active bottle reminders must be restored.

If notification permission is denied, the app must still work.

---

## UI and UX

Primary tabs:

1. Today
2. Logs
3. Insights
4. Settings

Today must prioritize:

- Baby selector.
- Active bottle card.
- New Bottle.
- Quick Feed.
- Quick Diaper.
- Quick Sleep.
- Today summary.

Night mode:

- Large buttons.
- Minimal text.
- Low-stimulation UI.
- No disruptive ads.
- No complex forms.
- Single-hand usage should be easy.

Accessibility:

- Support large font.
- Support TalkBack labels.
- Do not communicate status by color alone.
- Use clear text labels for states.

Compose rules:

- Hoist state.
- Keep Composables small.
- Avoid business logic in UI.
- Add previews for important screens.
- Support light and dark themes.

---

## Monetization

Free:

- 1 baby.
- Basic bottle timer.
- Basic logs.
- Today summary.
- Ads.
- Default widget.

Pro:

- No ads.
- Multiple babies.
- Full history.
- Advanced stats.
- Export.
- Backup.
- Custom reminders.
- Custom timer rules.
- Widget themes.

Suggested pricing:

- Monthly: USD 2.99
- Yearly: USD 19.99
- Lifetime: USD 29.99

Ads:

- Prefer banner/native only in MVP.
- Do not show disruptive ads in night mode.
- Do not show disruptive ads during active feeding.
- Do not show disruptive ads immediately after a bottle-expiry notification.
- Pro users must see no ads.

---

## Localization

Initial languages:

- English
- Spanish
- Simplified Chinese
- German
- French

Never hardcode user-facing strings in Kotlin.

All user-facing copy must use string resources.

Safety and disclaimer text must preserve the same meaning across languages.

Do not auto-switch guideline region based only on language.

---

## Privacy

Do not request unnecessary permissions.

Do not request:

- Location
- Contacts
- Camera
- Microphone

Do not collect:

- Baby real names as required data.
- Medical diagnosis.
- Notes content in analytics.
- Detailed health concerns.

Encourage baby nicknames.

MVP data should be local-first.

Cloud backup must be opt-in if added.

---

## Analytics

Allowed analytics events include:

- onboarding_started
- baby_created
- guideline_selected
- notification_permission_shown
- notification_permission_granted
- bottle_created
- bottle_started_feeding
- bottle_refrigerated
- bottle_expired
- bottle_discarded
- feed_logged
- diaper_logged
- sleep_started
- sleep_ended
- widget_added
- paywall_viewed
- purchase_started
- purchase_completed
- purchase_failed
- export_clicked
- backup_enabled
- language_changed

Do not log baby names, notes, or sensitive health content.

---

## Testing

Add or maintain tests for:

- Formula room-temperature expiry.
- Formula feeding-started expiry.
- Formula refrigerated expiry.
- Breast milk room-temperature expiry.
- Breast milk refrigerated expiry.
- Bottle state transitions.
- Notification scheduling and cancellation.
- Unit conversion.
- Today summary.
- Cross-day logs.

When changing bottle timer logic, update tests.

When changing user-facing safety copy, check compliance wording.

When changing notifications, test app restart and device reboot behavior.

---

## Definition of Done

A change is complete only if:

- Code compiles.
- Relevant tests pass.
- User-facing strings are localized.
- No medical or safety guarantee is introduced.
- Bottle timer behavior is not broken.
- Notifications are handled correctly.
- Accessibility is not worsened.
- Light and dark themes still work.
- Pro users do not see ads.
- Night mode is not interrupted by ads.

---

## Non-Goals for MVP

Do not add:

- AI doctor
- Medical diagnosis
- Community feed
- Online pediatric consultation
- Baby photo analysis
- Growth abnormality detection
- Vaccine medical advice
- Real-time family sharing
- Complex account system
- Hardware integration
- Formula brand recommendations

Unless explicitly requested by the product owner.
